{"repositoryId":1279816624,"availability":"available","full":"ProfRino/crowd-count","name":"crowd-count","description":"Browser-only crowd-size estimator: polygon × density on a map or floor plan, with codified safety thresholds. Vue 3 + MapLibre + Turf.js, no backend.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Vue","stars":8,"forks":2,"created":"2026-06-25T03:24:41Z","updated":"2026-07-17T06:37:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://profrino.github.io/crowd-count/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:42.857Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:42.857Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:42.857Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T18:04:42.857Z","stars":8,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Crowd Count is a browser-only crowd-size estimator. Draw a polygon on a real-world map or an uploaded indoor floor plan, pick a crowd density — uniform or a linear gradient — and the tool multiplies area by density and benchmarks the estimate against codified safety thresholds (UK Purple Guide, Green Guide, NFPA 101, Still's upper safe limit). Version 2.0 adds a full 3D site view with instanced crowds, optional Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles, and animated 3D density references.","The whole tool runs entirely in your web browser. There is no installation, no backend, no Python environment, and no build step.","Disclaimer: No responsibility is taken for the use or output of this tool. All results are Fermi-style order-of-magnitude estimates and must be independently verified by a qualified safety professional before use in any design, planning, or regulatory context."],"features":["Pure client-side — no installation, no backend. The entire app builds to a static dist/ folder you can drop on GitHub Pages, Cloudflare Pages, Netlify or any CDN.","Outdoor mode. MapLibre GL JS on top of","OpenStreetMap tiles, with a free Esri satellite imagery toggle, optional Google roadmap and satellite basemaps (bring your own API key), an OSM Nominatim search box, and a live metric/imperial scale bar.","Indoor mode. Upload any JPG/PNG floor plan, click two points, enter a","known real-world distance, and the image becomes a calibrated drawing surface in true m² (or ft²)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ProfRino/crowd-count/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f5a1cff1bc1e75b2d8d04a7dbf95346eabeab029d45a561e4cf662b68b81b97e","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:43.007Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:43.007Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Crowd Count is a browser-only crowd-size estimator. Draw a polygon on a real-world map or an uploaded indoor floor plan, pick a crowd density — uniform or a linear gradient — and the tool multiplies area by density and benchmarks the estimate against codified safety thresholds (UK Purple Guide, Green Guide, NFPA 101, Still's upper safe limit). Version 2.0 adds a full 3D site view with instanced crowds, optional Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles, and animated 3D density references.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ProfRino/crowd-count/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"OpenStreetMap tiles, with a free Esri satellite imagery toggle, optional Google roadmap and satellite basemaps (bring your own API key), an OSM Nominatim search box, and a live metric/imperial scale bar.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ProfRino/crowd-count/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"You have two equally simple ways to run the app — both with no installation, no account, and no server.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ProfRino/crowd-count/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f5a1cff1bc1e75b2d8d04a7dbf95346eabeab029d45a561e4cf662b68b81b97e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ProfRino/crowd-count/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:43.007Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-17T06:37:42Z","readmeSnapshot":{"versio